    "result": "`add_business_days` is implemented in `solution.py`, and the six tests I wrote in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. It follows the spec. It validates the types first, rejecting `datetime`, `bool` and `float` values and holidays that aren't plain dates. It then steps day by day, skipping weekends and holidays. `n == 0` returns `start` if it is a business day and otherwise the next one. The tests cover forward and backward moves, zero, holidays (including weekend holidays and generators), and the `TypeError` cases.",
